From: SamuriHL CE22 build
Subject: [PATCH] rpu: synthesise L8 trims from CMv2.9 L2 on CMv4.0 append

Appending CMv4.0 metadata (dovi_rpu_add_cmv40_safe_default_metadata)
inserts L3/L9/L254/L11 but no L8. Once L254 marks the RPU as CM v4.0,
the DM computes its trims from L8 ONLY (see the level8.rs doc comment)
and ignores the source L2 - so the append silently destroys the
stream's authored trims (hardware-confirmed: DM tone LUT pinned to the
neutral curve while the stream's trim_offset ramps).

Add dovi_rpu_add_cmv40_metadata_with_l8_trims: same safe-default append,
plus one length-10 L8 block synthesised per CMv2.9 L2 target. Trim
transfer policy, derived from dual-authored (L2+L8, same target) studio
content: offset/chroma_weight/saturation_gain/ms_weight copy verbatim
(Dolby's own tools carry them 1:1; negative/unused ms_weight maps to
neutral 2048); slope/power are engine-dependent v2.9-curve compensation
and retain only 1/16 of their deviation from neutral (matches the
studio's own v4.0 values within ~0.5% on the measured sample). The
target display becomes the nearest preset index in PQ space, so no
authored L10 is needed; the L8-only fields with no L2 source are
omitted via length 10.
Returns 2 = added with L8, 1 = added (no L2), 0 = already CMv4.0,
-1 = error.

---
diff --git a/dolby_vision/src/capi.rs b/dolby_vision/src/capi.rs
index 619492a..b4cc275 100644
--- a/dolby_vision/src/capi.rs
+++ b/dolby_vision/src/capi.rs
@@ -476,6 +476,42 @@ pub unsafe extern "C" fn dovi_rpu_add_cmv40_safe_default_metadata(ptr: *mut RpuO
     }
 }
 
+/// # Safety
+/// The struct pointer must be valid.
+///
+/// Adds default CMv4.0 extension metadata (L3, L9, L11, L254) to the RPU,
+/// plus L8 trim blocks synthesised from the RPU's CMv2.9 L2 trims so the
+/// CM v4.0 DM keeps the authored trims (with no L8 present, a v4.0 DM
+/// ignores the source L2 and the trims fall back to neutral).
+/// Does nothing if CMv4.0 metadata is already present.
+///
+/// Returns 2 if metadata was added with L8 synthesised from L2, 1 if
+/// metadata was added with no L2 trims to carry over, 0 if CMv4.0 was
+/// already present, -1 on error.
+/// If an error occurs, it is logged to RpuOpaque.error.
+#[unsafe(no_mangle)]
+pub unsafe extern "C" fn dovi_rpu_add_cmv40_metadata_with_l8_trims(ptr: *mut RpuOpaque) -> i32 {
+    if ptr.is_null() {
+        return -1;
+    }
+
+    let opaque = unsafe { &mut *ptr };
+
+    if let Some(rpu) = &mut opaque.rpu {
+        match rpu.add_cmv40_safe_metadata_with_l8_trims() {
+            Ok(ret) => ret as i32,
+            Err(e) => {
+                opaque.error =
+                    CString::new(format!("Failed setting CMv4.0 metadata with L8 trims: {e}"))
+                        .ok();
+                -1
+            }
+        }
+    } else {
+        -1
+    }
+}
